    "summary": "Turn 38 reviewed the owner-alive protection check, whose outcome is holds.\n\nState on entry. Claim C5-noop-commit-reproposes-admitted-operation has one artifact, fb1d0e558f4641c7850fe8aaca4068df (executed as 975ffcb0…), whose monitor outcome is holds with the oracle correspondence unreviewed. Its retained stream prints proposal_admitted with bookkeeping true and pending 1, then noop_commit_at_owner with instance_status 4 (COMMITTED), pending_after 0 and reproposed_on_channel 1.\n\nReview judgement (checker_correspondence, no_issue_found). Requirement versus predicate: the claim is that the owner installs a single-NONE commit and re-proposes the admitted operation instead of dropping it, and the predicate asserts reproposed_on_channel == 1 on the commit event, evaluated on printed fields rather than a derived boolean. Entry and message legality: the operation is admitted by the real handlePropose (which attaches the proposal to the instance bookkeeping and broadcasts the PreAccept) and the commit is the one a recoverer broadcasts after restarting phase 1 with NOOP for the owner's instance, on the ordinary owner-alive record state. Oracle: the three printed quantities together distinguish re-proposal from dropping, since the pending list is cleared and one proposal is waiting on the channel. Identity: the admission prerequisite and the commit event share instance 0.0. Observation path and completion: both handlers are synchronous and their effects are read immediately, so no wait or cleanup duty is implied. Alternatives and reservations are explicit: the claim's scope deliberately excludes the restarted-owner case, where the same handler instead dereferences absent bookkeeping and terminates the replica, which is confirmed separately as claim C4; and the limitations record that the re-proposed operation's later commit, execution and client reply are not driven and that the commit is delivered directly rather than through the run loop.\n\nEffect. If accepted, the pair is complete for this handler: C4 confirms the crash when bookkeeping is absent, C5 confirms the protection when it is present, so the earlier client-completion suspicion is delimited — an admitted operation survives a NOOP commit while its owner lives, and the only remaining client-side gap is the driver client's lack of retry, already recorded on the active candidate. Audit spec version 7; the four earlier confirmed claims are untouched, the accept-status candidate stays paused, and the scope-issue bookkeeping debt remains visible. No requirement, premise or earlier observation was weakened."
